            <ArticleTitle>Hemophagocytic syndrome in pregnancy: case report, diagnosis, treatment, and prognosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1756-1764</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccr3.1172</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Diagnosis of hemophagocytic syndrome remains a challenge in particular during pregnancy. Concomitant presence of clinical and biological signs, for example, fever, pancytopenia, hyperferritinemia, and hypertriglyceridemia, should alert clinicians to suspect HPS and proceed to prompt treatments.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
